# Everything in this repo is consumed by Linux: shell scripts run under bash,
# Ansible reads YAML inside a build VM, and Packer HCL is parsed on a Linux
# builder. A CRLF checkout breaks all of it in confusing ways -- a script's
# shebang becomes "bash\r", which fails with "No such file or directory" while
# the file is plainly there.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree means a clone on Windows, or into a Windows
# filesystem under WSL, produces files that actually run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a stray \r is fatal rather than cosmetic.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.hcl   text eol=lf
*.j2    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
